From: Paullo9 <paullobpreis@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:44:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] N_V estimator with typed thickness and its synthetic truth
 harness (tier 1; Core only, no UI, no state, nothing wired in):
 PrecipitateNumberDensity.estimate (per-object, exact edge weight, h per
 class, three sigma terms, refusals, validation "none");
 tools/number-density-test (point-sampled, size-biased lognormal, 54 cells)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tests first: 8 of 9 red on a stub (the 9th, the length-sigma finite difference, passes vacuously on zeros), green on the code (9/9). Mutations, each red: N/(A t) form (6 tests), edge weight 1 (4), sigma_L without s (1), T1 s = 1 (2), sigma_t slope without (t+h) (3), Poisson term linear (1). Harness run (docs/archive/v5/number-density-run1-2026-10-15.log): registered gate FAILS as the design note predicted: P1 refuted at theta' d100 t100 (1.074), theta' d190 t200 (1.064), T1 d190 t200 (1.058); P2 cells outside the bar; naive fails every d >= 100 cell; 54/54 cells within +-0.05 of the note's table. Deviation from design §3 wording: plates carry a physical thickness of one pixel (zero-thickness edge-on plates are measure zero under point sampling); chord length is exact. Item closes per ADR 050.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
